ng vulnerable PaperCut NG/MF servers.\nL17: \nL18:     * cite1†Bill Toulas L19:     * September 10, 2026\nL20:     * 11:55 AM\nL21:     * cite4†1 L22: \nL23:   * #### cite5†Webinar: How AI broke the Pyramid of Pain†pushsecurity.com ^{cite6†Image†www.bleepstatic.com }\nL24: The Pyramid of Pain works on the core idea that the higher your detections are up the pyramid, the harder you are to evade. But AI has collapsed the value of the bottom layers to zero.\nL25: \nL26: The latest webinar from Push Security explains how this change impacts detection and response, and what security teams can do about it.\nL27: \nL28:     * cite5†Push Security†pushsecurity.com Sponsorship\nL29: \nL30:   * #### cite7†US says Chinese firms extracted billions of tokens from frontier AI models L31: U.S. cybersecurity and intelligence agencies say that six Chinese AI companies conducted industrial-scale distillation attacks on American frontier AI models since at least late 2024.\nL32: \nL33:     * cite1†Bill Toulas L34:     * September 09, 2026\nL35:     * 12:48 PM\nL36:     * cite8†0 L37: \nL38:   * #### cite9†OpenAI says GPT-6 Astra can find zero-days, but is also harder to monitor L39: \nL40: OpenAI confirmed that GPT-6 Astra is the first model it has broadly deployed to reach the \"Critical level\" for cybersecurity capabilities.\nL41:     * cite10†Mayank Parmar L42:     * September 08, 2026\nL43:     * 10:40 AM\nL44:     * cite11†1 L45: \nL46:   * #### cite12†Hackers build AI frameworks for widescale credential theft L47: \nL48: Threat actors are increasingly switching from AI-powered coding assistants to multi-agent frameworks that automate every stage of an attack.\nL49: \nL50:     * cite1†Bill Toulas L51:     * September 08, 2026\nL52:     * 08:03 AM\nL53:     * cite13†0 L54: \nL55:   * #### cite14†ChatGPT can now connect to your personal apps to mimic writing style L56: OpenAI appears to be testing a new \"Writing Style\" feature for ChatGPT that can learn how you write by looking at examples from your connected apps.\nL57: \nL58:     * cite10†Mayank Parmar L59:     * September 07, 2026\nL60:     * 06:36 AM\nL61:     * cite15†0 L62: \nL63:   * #### cite16†ChatGPT Astra is now rolling out to $20 Plus subscription L64: \nL65: OpenAI is now rolling out ChatGPT Astra, its most powerful model to date, to those with a $20 Plus subscription, but there's no word on when free users will get access..\nL66:     * cite10†Mayank Parmar L67:     * September 06, 2026\nL68:     * 09:15 PM\nL69:     * cite17†0 L70: \nL71:   * #### cite18†OpenAI confirms ChatGPT is down ahead of 'Astra' model launch L72: \nL73: ChatGPT and Codex are experiencing a major outage, with users reporting errors across nearly every major ChatGPT feature.\nL74: \nL75:     * cite10†Mayank Parmar L76:     * September 03, 2026\nL77:     * 11:13 AM\nL78:     * cite19†0 L79: \nL80:   * #### cite20†Anthropic confirms Claude is down, multiple models affected L81: Claude is experiencing an outage, with users encountering elevated errors when sending requests to multiple Anthropic AI models.\nL82: \nL83:     * cite10†Mayank Parmar L84:     * September 03, 2026\nL85:     * 11:02 AM\nL86:     * cite21†0 L87: \nL88:   * #### cite22†OpenAI confirms ChatGPT outage as users report errors L89: \nL90: ChatGPT Work is experiencing a partial outage, and users across multiple subscription plans may be unable to start or continue tasks.\nL91: \nL92:     * cite10†Mayank Parmar L93:     * August 31, 2026\nL94:     * 12:50 PM\nL95:     * cite23†0 L96:   * #### cite24†Anthropic warns infostealer malware is hijacking Claude sessions to drain usage L97: \nL98: Anthropic is warning some Claude users that infostealer malware on their PCs has stolen active Claude login sessions, allowing attackers to access accounts and consume their usage.\nL99: \nL100:     * cite10†Mayank Parmar L101:     * August 30, 2026\nL102:     * 10:30 AM\nL103:     * cite25†0 L104: \nL105:   * #### cite26†Anthropic is cutting Claude Code's current weekly limits by 17% L106: Anthropic is permanently increasing Claude Code's standard weekly usage limits by 25% for Pro, Max, Team, and seat-based Enterprise plans, but it's not as good as it sounds.\nL107: \nL108:     * cite10†Mayank Parmar L109:     * August 29, 2026\nL110:     * 07:11 PM\nL111:     * cite27†3 L112: \nL113:   * #### cite28†Nearly 700 rogue AI agents coordinated in the Hugging Face attack L114: New details about the July attack on Hugging Face reveal that hundreds of AI agents driven by OpenAI's internal IM1 model coordinated the compromise through an unauthorized message board.\nL115: \nL116:     * cite1†Bill Toulas L117:     * August 27, 2026\nL118:     * 05:38 PM\nL119:     * cite29†1 L120: \nL121:   * #### cite30†AnonyMousKIT PhaaS uses voice AI agents to phish iPhone passcodes L122: A newly uncovered phishing-as-a-service (PhaaS) platform called AnonyMousKIT automates the retrieval of codes used to unlock stolen Apple devices and disable the Activation Lock feature.\nL123: \nL124:     * cite1†Bill Toulas L125:     * August 25, 2026\nL126:     * 04:25 PM\nL127:     * cite31†0 L128: \nL129:   * #### cite32†OpenAI confirms ChatGPT is down as logins and signups fail L130: \nL131: ChatGPT is experiencing a major outage, and users are unable to sign in, create accounts, or load chats, including previous conversations.\n"
